WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.100
We have a hairy-looking
expression here.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.600
And your goal is to try to
simplify it as much as you can.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.600
And I'll give you a little
bit of time to do it.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.330
Let's just think about
it, step by step.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.610
And it might help if we
were to actually reorder

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.670
the terms in this expression.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.810
So let me put all
the x terms first.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:24.240
So I have 5x-- that's
that term-- minus 2x.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:32.060
Then I have plus 7y plus 3y.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:43.447
Then i have plus 8z,
and then I have minus z.

00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:45.530
And then the last term
that I haven't included yet

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.630
is that plus 5.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.440
Now we'll just think it through.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.885
If I have 5 x's and
I were to take away 2

00:00:55.885 --> 00:00:58.687
x's, is how many x's am
I going to be left with?

00:00:58.687 --> 00:01:00.270
Well, I'm going to
be left with 3 x's.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:01.269
That's true of anything.

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:03.920
There's not some fancy
algebraic magic going on here.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.615
5 of anything minus
2 of that same thing,

00:01:06.615 --> 00:01:08.490
you're going to be left
with 3 of that thing.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.210
In this case, that
thing are x's.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:17.126
So this is going
to simplify to 3x.

00:01:17.126 --> 00:01:18.500
Now, in a lot of
algebra classes,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.291
you'll hear people say,
oh, well, you know,

00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:23.930
the coefficient on 5x is 5.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.060
And the coefficient on
this subtracting the 2x,

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.640
the coefficient
here is negative 2,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.170
and we had to add
the coefficients.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:36.880
Let me write that word
down-- coefficient.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.840
These right over here
are the coefficients.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.810
They're the number that you're
multiplying the variable by.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.600
So you're the 5 or the
negative 2 in this case.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.100
And so you could
just say, oh, I had

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.705
to just add the coefficients.

00:01:48.705 --> 00:01:50.830
And that's OK, and there's
nothing wrong with that.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.621
But I really want to
emphasize that there's

00:01:52.621 --> 00:01:54.690
a very common sense
intuition here.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.930
If you have 5 of something, you
take away 2 of that something,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.570
you are left with 3
of that something.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.937
And you have to be very careful.

00:02:01.937 --> 00:02:04.270
You have to make sure that
you're adding and subtracting

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.090
the same things.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.440
Here, we're dealing with x's.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.430
So we can take 5 x's
and take away 2 x's.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.910
We can't think about merging
the x's and the y's, at least

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.870
not in any simple way right
now, because that, frankly,

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.070
wouldn't make any
intuitive sense.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.340
Now let's think about the y's.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.824
If I have 7 of something,
and I were to add 3 more

00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:24.240
of that something,
well, then, I'm

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.780
going to have 10
of that something.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:31.420
So this part right over here
is going to simplify to 10y.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.030
Once again, you could say
the coefficient on 7y is 7.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.260
The coefficient on 3y is 3.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.900
We added the coefficients--
7 plus 3-- to get 10y.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.147
But I really want to
emphasize the intuition here.

00:02:43.147 --> 00:02:45.730
It's much more if you've got 7
of something, you add another 3

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.910
to that something, you've
got 10 of that something.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.470
Now let's look at the z's.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:53.197
If I've got 8 of something
and I take away 1 of them,

00:02:53.197 --> 00:02:54.780
I'm going to have 7
of that something.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.222
So that is 7z.

00:02:56.222 --> 00:02:57.430
And you might say, hey, wait.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.721
What was the coefficient
right here on this negative z?

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:02.040
I don't see any number
out front of the z.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.087
Well, implicitly, I
could have put a 1 here,

00:03:04.087 --> 00:03:05.420
and it's exactly the same thing.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.360
Subtracting a z is the exact
same thing as subtracting 1z.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.072
The word "onesie" strikes
a part of my brain

00:03:11.072 --> 00:03:12.530
because I have very
young children,

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:14.556
but that's a different
type of onesie.

00:03:14.556 --> 00:03:15.930
And then you could
see, oh, yeah,

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.090
you definitely did add the
two coefficients, the 8

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.415
and the negative 1.

00:03:20.415 --> 00:03:22.320
But once again,
common sense tells you

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.840
if you have 8 of something,
and you take away 1 of them,

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.720
you have 7 of that something.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.860
And then finally,
you have a plus 5.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:32.740
So we're done.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:41.980
This simplified to 3x
plus 10y plus 7z plus 5.

